abstract: >
  Scientists from NOAA's National Centers for Environmental Information (NCEI)
  and the Cooperative Institute for Research in Environmental Sciences (CIRES)
  led a hands-on introduction to open-source coastal DEM workflows. Using a
  hosted JupyterHub environment, participants inspected and ran a reproducible
  workflow for generating 1/9 arc-second coastal DEMs for Newport, Oregon, and
  Sarasota, Florida. The workshop demonstrated how tools from the Continuous
  DEMs project support source-data access, processing, vertical datum
  harmonization, DEM generation, and independent validation. This workshop
  built on the April 16, 2026 webinar, "Open-Source Workflows for Coastal DEM
  Generation."

